Privacy Policy for AI Digger - Smart Web Scraper
Last Updated: March 29, 2026

1. Introduction Welcome to AI Digger ("we," "our," or "us"). We are committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how our Chrome Extension, AI Digger, collects, uses, and safeguards your information.

AI Digger is designed with a "Privacy First" and "Local First" architecture. We do not have access to your scraped data, your API keys, or your browsing history.

2. Information We Collect and How We Use It To provide our web scraping and AI automation features, the extension processes certain data strictly within your local browser environment:

Scraped Data & Website Content: When you initiate a scraping job, the extension reads the content of the active web page to extract the data you requested. This data is temporarily stored in your browser's local storage, allowing you to download it (in CSV/Excel format) or send it to your configured webhooks.

Authentication Information (API Keys): To use the AI features, you must provide your own API keys (OpenAI, Gemini, or Claude). These keys are saved exclusively in your browser's secure chrome.storage.sync. We never transmit these keys to our servers.

User Activity (Macro Recording): If you use the Macro Recorder feature, the extension temporarily records your clicks and keystrokes on the active page to build your automation blueprint. This tracking only occurs when the recorder is visibly active.

Personally Identifiable Information (Feedback Form): If you click the "Feedback" button, the extension may request access to your Google Account email address (chrome.identity.email). This is used solely to optionally pre-populate the contact field on our Google Forms bug report page to save you time. We do not store or collect this email otherwise.

3. Third-Party Services and Data Sharing We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information or scraped data to third parties. Your data only leaves your browser under your explicit instructions:

LLM Providers: When using AI Inspector or Magic Build, HTML snippets are sent directly to the AI provider you configured (OpenAI, Google Gemini, or Anthropic Claude) using your personal API key.

Webhooks: If you configure a Webhook URL (e.g., Zapier, Make.com, or a custom API), the extension will transmit your extracted data directly to that URL.

4. Data Retention and Deletion Because your data is stored locally, you have complete control over it. You can delete your scraped data, saved job blueprints, and API keys at any time directly through the extension's UI or by uninstalling the extension.

5. Changes to This Privacy Policy We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by updating the "Effective Date" at the top of this policy.

